            <ArticleTitle>The role of symmetry breaking in the structural trapping of light-induced excited spin states.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13268-13271</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07990g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Light-Induced Excited Spin State Trapping (LIESST) data are reported for seven isostructural solvate salts from the iron(ii)/2,6-di(pyrazol-1-yl)pyridine family. A complicated relationship between their spin-crossover T1/2 and T(LIESST) values may reflect low-temperature thermal and light-induced symmetry breaking, which is shown by one of the compounds but not by two others.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
